{"success": true, "code": 200, "message": "Detection complete", "data": {"sentences": [], "isHuman": 0, "additional_feedback": "", "h": ["This pull request refactors the `handleStringData` method in `ImportHandler.java` to utilize `CompositeIdFetcher` for fetching bibliographic entries.", "The method now checks if the input string contains a valid identifier using `CompositeIdFetcher.containsValidId`.", "If a valid identifier is found, it attempts to fetch the corresponding bibliographic entry using `CompositeIdFetcher.performSearchById`.", "If no valid identifier is found, it falls back to trying various import formats using `tryImportFormats`.", "This change simplifies the method and leverages the capabilities of `CompositeIdFetcher` for handling different types of identifiers.", "Additionally, a no-args constructor was added to `CompositeFetcher.java` to allow the use of `performSearchById`, which is not a static method.", "Closes https://github.com/JabRef/jabref/issues/12004"], "hi": [], "textWords": 101, "aiWords": 101, "fakePercentage": 100.0, "specialIndexes": [], "specialSentences": [], "originalParagraph": "2026/2/17/bafde37b-6857-45ee-bbe5-e4fca282c3f3", "feedback": "Your Text is AI/GPT Generated", "input_text": "This pull request refactors the `handleStringData` method in `ImportHandler.java` to utilize `CompositeIdFetcher` for fetching bibliographic entries. The method now checks if the input string contains a valid identifier using `CompositeIdFetcher.containsValidId`. If a valid identifier is found, it attempts to fetch the corresponding bibliographic entry using `CompositeIdFetcher.performSearchById`. If no valid identifier is found, it falls back to trying various import formats using `tryImportFormats`. This change simplifies the method and leverages the capabilities of `CompositeIdFetcher` for handling different types of identifiers.

Additionally, a no-args constructor was added to `CompositeFetcher.java` to allow the use of `performSearchById`, which is not a static method.

Closes https://github.com/JabRef/jabref/issues/12004", "id": 44435671}}

{"success": true, "code": 200, "message": "Detection complete", "data": {"sentences": [], "isHuman": 100, "additional_feedback": "", "h": [], "hi": [], "textWords": 80, "aiWords": 0, "fakePercentage": 0.0, "specialIndexes": [], "specialSentences": [], "originalParagraph": "2026/2/16/a810ddd1-e2cc-4b1a-84c3-2e2df2e12011", "feedback": "Your Text is Human Written", "input_text": "Bugfix & UX: make global search safe when no database is open

- StateManager: Avoid potential NPE when querying search result size by returning a default SimpleIntegerProperty(0) if the active database is not present in searchResultMap. Added import for SimpleIntegerProperty. This ensures getSearchResultSize() always returns a valid IntegerProperty.

- GlobalSearchBar: Disable the search field when there is no open database by binding searchField.disableProperty() to needsDatabase(stateManager).not(). Added static import for needsDatabase. This improves UX by preventing search input when no database is available.", "id": 44399871}}

{"success": true, "code": 200, "message": "Detection complete", "data": {"sentences": [], "isHuman": 50, "additional_feedback": "", "h": ["The feature is based on the work initiated in #9263 and resolves #8729.", "A new option, 'Use System Preference,' has been added to the Preference -> General -> Appearance -> Visual Theme drop-down list.", "This option dynamically switches between light and dark themes based on the current OS settings.", "The implementation uses [jSystemThemeDetector](https://github.com/Dansoftowner/jSystemThemeDetector) to detect the system theme.", "Manual testing was conducted on both MacOS and Windows to ensure the theme changes as expected according to the system settings.", "The changes have been tested and verified on both operating systems, with a slight delay observed on an older Windows device during theme switching, which is assumed to be normal.", "Screenshots and videos demonstrating the feature are included in the PR.", "The `CHANGELOG.md` has been updated, and the feature is documented in the developer's documentation.", "For UI changes, relevant screenshots have been added to the PR description."], "hi": [], "textWords": 162, "aiWords": 146, "fakePercentage": 75.23, "specialIndexes": [], "specialSentences": [], "originalParagraph": "2026/2/17/50e63c72-2554-4f50-a28a-1f2f8ca929ed", "feedback": "Your Text contains mixed signals, with some parts generated by AI/GPT", "input_text": "This pull request adds an option to use the system preference for light/dark themes in JabRef. The feature is based on the work initiated in #9263 and resolves #8729. A new option, 'Use System Preference,' has been added to the Preference -> General -> Appearance -> Visual Theme drop-down list. This option dynamically switches between light and dark themes based on the current OS settings. The implementation uses [jSystemThemeDetector](https://github.com/Dansoftowner/jSystemThemeDetector) to detect the system theme.

