{"success": true, "code": 200, "message": "Detection complete", "data": {"sentences": [], "isHuman": 100, "additional_feedback": "", "h": ["} else if (importError instanceof ImportException) {", "DefaultTaskExecutor.runAndWaitInJavaFXThread(() -> dialogService.showWarningDialogAndWait(Localization.lang("Import error"), importError.getLocalizedMessage()));"], "hi": [], "textWords": 190, "aiWords": 12, "fakePercentage": 4.46, "specialIndexes": [15, 11, 1], "specialSentences": ["Result", "Notes", "Problem"], "originalParagraph": "2026/2/17/12bcdb9f-0fa5-495c-a2af-fd174b6fe331", "feedback": "Your Text is Human Written", "input_text": "Fixes #8011 — Show a meaningful warning when a .bib file has missing commas instead of an error dialog or silently showing an empty library.

Problem
- When importing or opening a malformed .bib file (e.g. missing commas) JabRef threw a generic ImportException and showed a full error stacktrace during import. When opening the library normally the UI showed an empty library with no message.

What this PR does
- Extracts and surfaces the parser error message from ParserResult and throws it as an ImportException so the user sees a meaningful message:
  throw new ImportException(parserResult.getErrorMessage());
- When the import error is an ImportException, show a warning dialog (not an error dialog):
  } else if (importError instanceof ImportException) {
      DefaultTaskExecutor.runAndWaitInJavaFXThread(() -> dialogService.showWarningDialogAndWait(Localization.lang("Import error"), importError.getLocalizedMessage()));
  }
- Applies the same handling to both import and file-opening flows so users get consistent feedback.

Notes
- Manually tested in a running JabRef instance.
- Screenshot added to the PR description showing the warning dialog.
- Tests and CHANGELOG update not included in this PR.

Result
- Users now receive a clear, actionable warning when a .bib file cannot be parsed due to missing commas or similar format issues, instead of an opaque exception or empty library.", "id": 44436282}}

